{"name":"White Sand","hex":"#f5ebd8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"sand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock that is ground more finely than gravel, but is not as fine as silt (more formally, see grain sizes chart), forming beaches and deserts and also used in construction.\n\n A specific grade, type, or composition of sand.\n\n A beach or other mass of sand.","A specific grade, type, or composition of sand."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light beige colour, like that of typical sand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whitesand Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Whitesand Bay is a wide sandy bay near Land's End in west Cornwall, England, United Kingdom. It stretches for one mile between the headlands of Pedn-mên-du and Aire Point. and contains the village of Sennen Cove. It is also a landing point for the Atlantic Crossing 1 international telecommunications cable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Sennen_Cove_beach_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1170431.jpg/330px-Sennen_Cove_beach_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1170431.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitesand_Bay"},{"title":"Whitesands Bay (Pembrokeshire)","blocks":[{"text":"Whitesands Bay is a Blue Flag beach situated on the St David's peninsula in the Pembrokeshire Coast National Park, Wales. Whitesand Bay, on some maps, located 2 miles (3.2 km) west of St. Davids and 1 mile (1.6 km) south of St Davids Head, has been described as the best surfing beach in Pembrokeshire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Porth_Mawr_%28Whitesands_Bay%29_near_Tyddewi_%28St_David%27s%29%2C_Sir_Benfro%2C_Cymru%2C_Wales_15.jpg/330px-Porth_Mawr_%28Whitesands_Bay%29_near_Tyddewi_%28St_David%27s%29%2C_Sir_Benfro%2C_Cymru%2C_Wales_15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitesands_Bay_(Pembrokeshire)"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Gwynver_Beach_-_high_tide_%287973546852%29.jpg/500px-Gwynver_Beach_-_high_tide_%287973546852%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Gwynver_Beach_-_high_tide_%287973546852%29.jpg/1280px-Gwynver_Beach_-_high_tide_%287973546852%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Gwynver_Beach_-_high_tide_%287973546852%29.jpg/500px-Gwynver_Beach_-_high_tide_%287973546852%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gwynver Beach","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGwynver_Beach_-_high_tide_(7973546852).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Carn_Llidi_%288397%29.jpg/500px-Carn_Llidi_%288397%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Carn_Llidi_%288397%29.jpg/1280px-Carn_Llidi_%288397%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Carn_Llidi_%288397%29.jpg/500px-Carn_Llidi_%288397%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carn Llidi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarn_Llidi_(8397).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Archaeological_dig_at_Porth_Mawr_%28recent_English_translation_-_%27Whitesands_Bay%27%29%2C_Sir_Benfro%2C_Cymru%2C_Wales_10.jpg/500px-Archaeological_dig_at_Porth_Mawr_%28recent_English_translation_-_%27Whitesands_Bay%27%29%2C_Sir_Benfro%2C_Cymru%2C_Wales_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Archaeological_dig_at_Porth_Mawr_%28recent_English_translation_-_%27Whitesands_Bay%27%29%2C_Sir_Benfro%2C_Cymru%2C_Wales_10.jpg/1280p